          "sourceDoi": "10.1103/physrevresearch.2.023173",
          "targetDoi": "10.1016/j.aop.2005.04.011",
          "snippet": "First, the dynamics of biological structures are challenged by the ubiquitous heavy dissipation [104][105][106]. It is worth applying non-Hermitian mechanics to active biological systems in which the heavy damping is counteracted by energy production, such as motor activities in fiber networks and motility of cell sheets.",
          "section": "summary and perspectives",
